      "hints": [
        "Subtract $u_2 - u_1 = -\\frac{\\tan^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} - \\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\theta}$.",
        "Replace $\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}$ to get $-\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^4\\theta} = -\\frac{1}{\\cos^4\\theta}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the common difference $d = u_2 - u_1$ of the arithmetic progression:\n$$d = -\\frac{\\tan^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} - \\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\theta}$$",
        "Substitute $\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}$ and write over the common denominator $\\cos^4\\theta$:\n$$d = -\\frac{\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}}{\\cos^2\\theta} - \\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\theta} = -\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^4\\theta} - \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^4\\theta} = -\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^4\\theta}$$",
        "Apply the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$:\n$$d = -\\frac{1}{\\cos^4\\theta}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
