      "hints": [
        "For $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$, find $a = \\frac{4}{3}$ and $d = -\\frac{16}{9}$.",
        "Evaluate $u_{13} = a + 12d = \\frac{4}{3} + 12\\left(-\\frac{16}{9}\\right)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate the first term $a$ and common difference $d$ at $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$ (noting $\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$):\n$$a = \\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{4}} = \\frac{4}{3}$$\n$$d = -\\frac{1}{\\cos^4\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)} = -\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2} = -\\frac{1}{\\frac{9}{16}} = -\\frac{16}{9}$$",
        "Apply the $n$th term formula for $n = 13$:\n$$u_{13} = a + (13 - 1)d = \\frac{4}{3} + 12\\left(-\\frac{16}{9}\\right) = \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{4 \\times 16}{3} = \\frac{4 - 64}{3} = -\\frac{60}{3} = -20$$"
      ],
